{"id":"Q1042","iso2":"SC","iso3":"SYC","name":"Seychelles","wiki":"Seychelles","description":"island sovereign state off the eastern coast of Africa","flag":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Flag_of_Seychelles.svg/330px-Flag_of_Seychelles.svg.png","capital":"Victoria","capitalCoord":[-4.623611111,55.454444444],"inception":"1976-06-29","government":[],"legislature":["National Assembly of Seychelles"],"continent":["Africa"],"website":"https://egov.sc","offices":[{"id":"Q18463915","role":"hog","title":"President of Seychelles"},{"id":"Q18463915","role":"hos","title":"President of Seychelles"}],"currentHog":"Q16190544","currentHos":"Q16190544","terms":[{"office":"Q18463915","roles":["hog","hos"],"person":"Q362948","start":"1976-06-29","end":"1977-06-05"},{"office":"Q18463915","roles":["hog","hos"],"person":"Q224986","start":"1977-06-05","end":"2004-04-16"},{"office":"Q18463915","roles":["hog","hos"],"person":"Q57476","start":"2004-04-16","end":"2016-10-16"},{"office":"Q18463915","roles":["hog","hos"],"person":"Q5220343","start":"2016-10-16","end":"2020-10-26"},{"office":"Q18463915","roles":["hog","hos"],"person":"Q1568174","start":"2020-10-26","end":null},{"office":"Q18463915","roles":["hog","hos"],"person":"Q16190544","start":"2025-10-26","end":null}],"people":{"Q362948":{"id":"Q362948","name":"James Mancham","desc":"President of Seychelles (1939-2017)","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/James_Mancham_2014.jpg/330px-James_Mancham_2014.jpg","gender":"M","born":"1939-08-11","died":"2017-01-08","birthplace":"Victoria","parties":["Seychelles Democratic Party"],"education":[],"occupations":["diplomat","politician"],"wiki":"James Mancham"},"Q224986":{"id":"Q224986","name":"France-Albert René","desc":"President of Seychelles (1935-2019)","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/France_Albert-Ren%C3%A9.png/330px-France_Albert-Ren%C3%A9.png","gender":"M","born":"1935-11-16","died":"2019-02-27","birthplace":"Victoria","parties":["United Seychelles Party"],"education":["King's College London","The Dickson Poon School of Law"],"occupations":["diplomat","politician","lawyer"],"wiki":"France-Albert René"},"Q57476":{"id":"Q57476","name":"James Michel","desc":"3rd President of Seychelles","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/James_Michel_2014.png/330px-James_Michel_2014.png","gender":"M","born":"1944-08-16","died":null,"birthplace":"Anse Boileau","parties":["United Seychelles Party"],"education":[],"occupations":["diplomat","politician"],"wiki":"James Michel"},"Q5220343":{"id":"Q5220343","name":"Danny Faure","desc":"4th President of Seychelles","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Danny_Faure_2010_Moscow_Unesco.jpg/330px-Danny_Faure_2010_Moscow_Unesco.jpg","gender":"M","born":"1962-05-08","died":null,"birthplace":"Kilembe","parties":["United Seychelles Party"],"education":[],"occupations":["politician","finance minister"],"wiki":"Danny Faure"},"Q1568174":{"id":"Q1568174","name":"Wavel Ramkalawan","desc":"Seychellois politician","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Wavel_Ramkalawan_-_president_of_Seychelles_(cropped).jpg/330px-Wavel_Ramkalawan_-_president_of_Seychelles_(cropped).jpg","gender":"M","born":"1961-03-15","died":null,"birthplace":"Mahé","parties":["Seychelles National Party","Linyon Demokratik Seselwa"],"education":["University of Birmingham"],"occupations":["politician","parson"],"wiki":"Wavel Ramkalawan"},"Q16190544":{"id":"Q16190544","name":"Patrick Herminie","desc":"Seychellois politician","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Patrick_Herminie_-_President_of_Seychelles_(cropped).jpg/330px-Patrick_Herminie_-_President_of_Seychelles_(cropped).jpg","gender":"M","born":"1963-09-22","died":null,"birthplace":"Praslin","parties":["United Seychelles Party"],"education":["University of Leeds","Charles University"],"occupations":["politician"],"wiki":"Patrick Herminie"}},"summary":"Seychelles ( , ; French: [sɛʃɛl] or [seʃɛl]), officially the Republic of Seychelles (French: République des Seychelles; Seychellois Creole: Repiblik Sesel), is an archipelagic country consisting of 115 islands in the Indian Ocean. Its capital and largest city, Victoria, is 1,500 kilometres (800 nautical miles) east of mainland Africa. Nearby island countries and territories include the Maldives, Comoros, Madagascar, Mauritius, and the French overseas departments of Mayotte and Réunion to the south; and the Chagos Archipelago to the east.\nSeychelles is the smallest country in Africa as well as the least populated sovereign African country, with an estimated population of 100,600 in 2022.\nThe Seychelles archipelago was uninhabited prior to sustained external contact. Arab sailors knew of the islands through Indian Ocean trade routes and they are described in medieval Arabic books. In the 16th century, Europeans described the islands, but they remained without permanent settlement until the 18th century, when France formally claimed them. During the period of French colonization, enslaved Africans were brought to the islands for plantation labor; many had already been captured and enslaved through existing African-Arab slave trade or Indian Ocean slave trade.\nIt faced competing French and British interests until it came under full British control in the early 19th century. After Britain assumed control, slavery was abolished and later replaced in part by indentured laborers from India. Since proclaiming independence from the United Kingdom in 1976, it has developed from a largely agricultural society to a market-based diversified economy, characterized by service, public sector, and tourism activities. From 1976 to 2015, nominal GDP grew nearly 700%, and purchasing power parity nearly 1600%. Since the late 2010s, the government has taken steps to encourage foreign investment.\nAs of the early 21st century, Seychelles has the highest nominal per capita GDP and the highest Human Development Index ranking of any African country. According to the 2024 V-Dem Democracy indices, Seychelles is the 43rd-ranked electoral democracy worldwide, the 1st-ranked liberal democracy in Africa, and the 2nd-ranked electoral democracy on the continent. Seychellois culture and society is an eclectic mix of French, British, Indian and African influences, with infusions of Chinese elements. The country is a member of the United Nations, the African Union, the Southern African Development Community, and the Commonwealth of Nations.","history":"The history of Seychelles dates back to the fourth of the Portuguese India Armadas led by Vasco da Gama, though Seychelles was likely already known to Arab navigators and other sailors for many centuries. On 15 March 1503, the scrivener Thomé Lopes noted the sighting of an elevated island, doubtless one of the granitic islands and almost certainly Silhouette Island. The first recorded landing was by the men of the English East India Company ship Ascension, which arrived in Seychelles in January 1609. The islands were claimed by France in 1756. Seychelles remained uninhabited until the first settlers arrived on board the ship Thélemaque, which arrived on 27 August 1770. Captain Leblanc Lecore landed the first colonists, comprising 15 white men, eight Africans and five Indians. The Seychellois Creole language developed as a means of communication between the different races. The British frigate Orpheus commanded by Captain Henry Newcome arrived at Mahé on 16 May 1794. Terms of capitulation were drawn up and the next day Seychelles was surrendered to Britain. Following the fall of Mauritius to British forces, Captain Phillip Beaver of the Nisus arrived at Mahé on 23 April 1811 and took possession of Seychelles as a permanent colony of Britain. The Seychelles became an independent republic in 1976. Following a coup d'état, a socialist one-party state ruled the country from 1977 to 1993. The subsequent democratic Presidential elections were won by candidates of the same party.","historyTitle":"History of Seychelles","curated":null,"indicators":{"gdp":[[1960,12012000],[1961,11592000],[1962,12642000],[1963,13923000],[1964,15393000],[1965,15603000],[1966,16443000],[1967,16632000],[1968,16074000],[1969,16452000],[1970,18432000],[1971,21966000],[1972,30645100],[1973,36896300],[1974,43134500],[1975,47803100],[1976,49279000],[1977,64526400],[1978,85552400],[1979,127261000],[1980,156784000],[1981,163751000],[1982,157212000],[1983,156098000],[1984,160993000],[1985,179691000],[1986,221147000],[1987,265213000],[1988,301986000],[1989,324333000],[1990,392164000],[1991,398307000],[1992,461409000],[1993,504231000],[1994,517570000],[1995,540733000],[1996,535250000],[1997,598967000],[1998,647287000],[1999,662839000],[2000,654212000],[2001,662064000],[2002,742135000],[2003,750847000],[2004,893012000],[2005,977899000],[2006,1081440000],[2007,1077310000],[2008,979597000],[2009,850902000],[2010,981617000],[2011,1058920000],[2012,1089410000],[2013,1333160000],[2014,1387580000],[2015,1432400000],[2016,1568510000],[2017,1675370000],[2018,1784310000],[2019,1868690000],[2020,1382550000],[2021,1487170000],[2022,1999890000],[2023,2171550000],[2024,2228610000],[2025,2387020000]],"population":[[1960,41700],[1961,42889],[1962,44042],[1963,45176],[1964,46322],[1965,47500],[1966,48699],[1967,49911],[1968,51134],[1969,52365],[1970,53600],[1971,54695],[1972,56029],[1973,56892],[1974,57937],[1975,59292],[1976,60504],[1977,61786],[1978,62150],[1979,62686],[1980,63261],[1981,64035],[1982,64413],[1983,64335],[1984,64717],[1985,65244],[1986,65652],[1987,68499],[1988,68755],[1989,69167],[1990,69507],[1991,70439],[1992,70763],[1993,72253],[1994,74205],[1995,75304],[1996,76417],[1997,77319],[1998,78846],[1999,80410],[2000,81131],[2001,81202],[2002,83723],[2003,82781],[2004,82475],[2005,82858],[2006,84600],[2007,85033],[2008,86956],[2009,87298],[2010,89770],[2011,87441],[2012,88303],[2013,89949